{"grade":"G9","deck_count":10,"decks":[{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":1,"title":"Set Theory","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"What is a set?","body":"A set is a well-defined collection of objects. We write A = {1, 2, 3}.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Roster vs set-builder","body":"Roster lists elements. Set-builder: {x | x is even, x < 10}.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Union & intersection","body":"A ∪ B = in A or B or both. A ∩ B = in both.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked example","body":"A={1,2,3}, B={3,4} → A∪B={1,2,3,4}, A∩B={3}.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"A={a,b}, B={b,c,d}. A∪B={a,b,c,d}, A∩B={b}.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":2,"title":"Foundation of Functions","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Relation vs function","body":"A function assigns each input exactly one output.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Domain & range","body":"Domain = allowed inputs. Range = actual outputs. f(x)=√x needs x≥0.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Function notation","body":"f(x)=2x+1 → f(3)=7.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked example","body":"f(x)=x²−1. f(2)=f(−2)=3.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"g(x)=3x−4. g(0)=−4, g(2)=2.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":3,"title":"Linear Functions","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Slope","body":"m=(y2−y1)/(x2−x1). Positive slope rises to the right.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Slope-intercept","body":"y=mx+b. m=slope, b=y-intercept.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Worked example","body":"Through (0,1) and (2,5): m=2 → y=2x+1.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Parallel & perpendicular","body":"Parallel: same m. Perpendicular: m1·m2=−1.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"Slope of y=−3x+7 is −3.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":4,"title":"Quadratic Functions","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Standard form","body":"y=ax²+bx+c, a≠0. Graph is a parabola.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Vertex","body":"x=−b/(2a). Opens up if a>0.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Worked example","body":"y=x²−4x+3. Vertex at (2,−1).","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":4,"heading":"Roots","body":"Solutions of ax²+bx+c=0 via factoring or formula.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"y=−x²+1 opens downward.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":5,"title":"Exponential and Logarithmic Expressions","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Exponent rules","body":"a^m·a^n=a^(m+n). (a^m)^n=a^(mn). a^0=1.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Negative exponents","body":"a^(−n)=1/a^n. 2^(−3)=1/8.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Log idea","body":"log_b a=c means b^c=a.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked example","body":"2^3·2^2=32. log_2 8=3.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"3^0=1 and 5^(−1)=1/5.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":6,"title":"Right Angled Triangle and Trigonometric Ratios","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"SOH-CAH-TOA","body":"sin=opp/hyp, cos=adj/hyp, tan=opp/adj.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Pythagoras","body":"a²+b²=c² for right triangles.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Worked example","body":"3-4-5 triangle: sin opposite 3 is 3/5.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Special angles","body":"30-60-90 and 45-45-90 side ratios.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"In 3-4-5, cos adjacent to 4 is 4/5.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":7,"title":"Business Mathematics","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Percent change","body":"Increase=(new−old)/old×100%.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Simple interest","body":"I=PRT (rate as yearly decimal).","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Worked example","body":"P=1000, R=0.05, T=2 → I=100.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Profit & loss","body":"Profit when SP>CP.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"CP=200, SP=250 → profit 25%.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"MATH","unit_number":8,"title":"Polynomials","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Degree","body":"Highest power with nonzero coefficient.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Add/subtract","body":"Combine like terms only.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Multiply","body":"(x+1)(x+2)=x²+3x+2.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked example","body":"(2x²+3)+(x²−5)=3x²−2.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"Degree of 7x³−x+1 is 3.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"PHYSICS","unit_number":1,"title":"Physical Quantities and Measurement","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"SI base units","body":"Mass kg, length m, time s. Force unit newton = kg·m/s².","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Scalar vs vector","body":"Scalars: magnitude only. Vectors: magnitude and direction.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Precision tip","body":"Always write the unit with the number.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked idea","body":"3.5 km = 3500 m.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"Displacement is a vector; temperature is a scalar.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G9","subject":"PHYSICS","unit_number":2,"title":"Motion in a Straight Line","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Speed vs velocity","body":"Speed is scalar; velocity is vector (displacement/time).","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Acceleration","body":"a=Δv/Δt. Unit m/s².","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Equations of motion","body":"v=u+at; s=ut+½at²; v²=u²+2as (constant a).","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked idea","body":"u=0, a=2 m/s², t=3 s → v=6 m/s, s=9 m.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"20→10 m/s in 5 s → a=−2 m/s².","accent":"#DB2777"}]}]}
